  "title": "BNCI 2014-001 Motor Imagery dataset",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from nine healthy participants performing cued motor imagery of the left hand, right hand, feet, and tongue. It corresponds to BCI Competition IV Dataset 2a, a widely used benchmark for four-class motor imagery classification. Each participant completed two sessions of six runs, recorded with 22 EEG and 3 EOG channels at 250 Hz. The data are distributed in a BIDS-formatted derivative produced with MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BrainAmp MR plus amplifier and an EASYCAP cap using Ag/AgCl electrodes (22 EEG and 3 EOG channels, left mastoid reference) at 250 Hz, with an online bandpass of 0.05-200 Hz. Each session had 6 runs. Participants performed cued motor imagery of left hand, right hand, feet, or tongue after arrow cues, without feedback. Each subject had 200 training trials and 240 test trials.",
